// A capitalized name after a scalar type is read as one of its limits, as `MaxValue` is, in any
// script: `Ωmega` is reported as `Omega` is, and a lowercase `ωmega` is not.
// error: `int` has no member `Ωmega`
// error: `int` has no member `Omega`
// error: `int` is not defined

main()
    val a = int.Ωmega
    val b = int.Omega
    val c = int.ωmega
